brain tissue lost (e.g., aphasia, apraxia, disturbances in perceptual-motor function).","id":48,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,283.65,539.89,367.65],"firstLineX":90.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b18","kind":"heading","spans":[{"t":"Associated Features","id":49,"b":true,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,382.89,206.9,396.69],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b19","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"t":"The diagnosis may also be supported by subtle neurological signs (e.g., multiple primitive","id":50,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"reflexes such as glabellar sign, snout response, palmomental reflex) or deficits in saccades and","id":51,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"smooth-pursuit eye movements co-occurring with frontally mediated cognitive impairments such","id":52,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"as complex attention problems, slow processing speed, impaired memory retrieval, or executive","id":53,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"dysfunction. Particularly in some cases of penetrating TBI, the diagnosis of NCD due to TBI","id":54,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"may be supported by posttraumatic epilepsy with focal onset in a location that corresponds to the","id":55,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"anatomy of a cognitive domain in which an individual demonstrates impairment (e.g., medial","id":56,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"temporal lobe–onset seizures and episodic memory impairment; frontal lobe seizures and","id":57,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"executive dysfunction or social cognitive impairment).","id":58,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,403.65,539.91,530.85],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b20","kind":"heading","spans":[{"t":"Prevalence","id":59,"b":true,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,546.09,144.83,559.89],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b21","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"t":"The prevalence of major and mild NCD due to TBI varies with injury severity and time since","id":60,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"injury, with the highest frequencies among individuals with more severe injury and during the","id":61,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"acute/subacute post-injury period. In the United States, more than 2.87 million TBIs occur","id":62,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"annually, including more than 837,000 TBIs in children. These TBIs account for 2.5 million","id":63,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"emergency department visits, 288,000 hospitalizations, and more than 56,000","id":64,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,566.85,539.87,636.45],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b22","kind":"marker","spans":[{"t":"709","id":65,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[297.0,650.85,315.0,662.85],"firstLineX":297.0,"indent":60,"small":false},{"id":"b23","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"t":"deaths annually. Among individuals presenting to an emergency department with TBI, the rates","id":66,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"for men are 547.6 per 100,000 and for women are 385.9 per 100,000. The TBI rate is higher for","id":67,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"men than women in every age group up to age 75 years, after which the rates of TBI between","id":68,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,677.25,539.96,718.05],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false}],"figures":[],"ocr":null,"nativeTextSha256":"6f3a65b05a7ecbdc04ce7f78d5f14ca81762823a698e4c1bc64e1be9919fb2e3","nativeCharacters":2940,"sparse":false,"tableCount":0}